message:
plugin-catalog: add operations

Maintainer copy of #136857 by @c-pompa (the PR is a draft its author can't mark ready);
YAML byte-identical to the PR head at pin 61b5e241.

fix(plugins): keep aliases and whole user information in bundle sources

Address the second ds-review-bot round on the bundle Source section:

- remove an http(s) URL's user information up to its last `@`, so a
  username containing `@` no longer leaves the password behind;
- keep the dependency name before a local or git spec when the package's
  own manifest name differs, so reinstalling restores the alias;
- accept scp-like git addresses with any user name;
- show Built in for a profile dependency whose loaded copy the
  installation supplies, instead of hiding the section;
- align the PackageView, subsystem page, and README wording with the
  shadowing rule and the kept query string, and assert the source of
  not-bundle and unreadable bundles.

fix(plugins): keep credentials and shadowed copies out of bundle sources

Address the first ds-review-bot round on the bundle Source section:

- strip the user information of http(s) and git+http(s) URLs so a private
  Git URL's token reaches neither the page nor the plugin_manager tool;
- expand `~` in file:/link: paths to the home directory as pnpm does;
- write jsr: aliases after the dependency name, like npm: aliases;
- give no source for a profile dependency the installation also supplies,
  whose installation copy is the one that loads;
- label the English row "Code source" to match the Chinese copy and hold
  for built-in bundles, and sync the subsystem page, READMEs, CSS comment,
  and tool test.

i18n(desktop): translate cron.queuedRun in every overlay

Main added the Run History 'Queued run' label (44c1ad7f84) in English only;
this branch's overlay-completeness ratchet fails on a new untranslated key.

fix(pm): spell store roots PM opens without Store like Store does

Some PM code reaches a store root from paths.store_root() or
writable_store_root() directly instead of through Store, so its file
calls kept the ordinary spelling and stay cut at MAX_PATH on Windows
with LongPathsEnabled=0. Worse, its comparisons against a Store root
(now \\?\-spelled) never matched.

Each such root now gets long_root() once, where the variable is born:
- Facts.refresh_digests digests whole payload tool trees;
- verified_tools walks and digests the source store's tool trees;
- the uv cache seed copies the payload's deep uv-cache tree out;
- _toolchain's writable store, so `location.root != writable` compares
  like with like and the copy store is built from the same spelling;
- _installed_location passes store.root to Facts.installed;
- ensure() picks the shipped facts by comparing two Store roots;
- the corrupt-facts guard compares both sides spelled long.

Returned and exported paths stay ordinary (previous commit).

fix(code-health): measure every Python unit's real end line

compare.py's cross-file move matching slices the origin function by its end line;
without it the engine estimated the end from the line count. Pass ast's end_lineno through.

refactor(cron): import Future at module level in cronjob_tools

concurrent.futures is stdlib with no cycle or startup-cost reason to defer it;
the module already imports its other stdlib deps at the top.
